WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.760
Least privilege is the central design pattern.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:10.180
Run containers as a non-root user, prevent privilege escalation, and drop capabilities that the application does not require.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:19.200
Avoid privileged mode, host namespaces, host devices, runtime sockets, and broad host mounts unless a reviewed system function truly needs them.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:25.420
Use read-only root filesystems where practical and provide narrowly scoped writable volumes for required state.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:36.600
Protect secrets through dedicated management, short-lived delivery where supported, restricted service accounts, and avoidance of secrets baked into images or ordinary environment artifacts.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.620
Seccomp limits system calls available to a process.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:45.600
AppArmor and SELinux can constrain file, process, and resource access through mandatory policy.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:53.340
These controls complement namespaces and capabilities; profiles should be tested against real application behavior and maintained through updates.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:59.080
Apply Pod Security Standards and admission policies to enforce expected settings before deployment.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:06.900
Policy should verify image sources, user settings, capabilities, mounts, host access, and required profiles.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.280
Manage exceptions with owners, expiration, and compensating controls.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:22.460
Harden images by minimizing packages, removing unsafe defaults, using trusted base images, scanning and signing artifacts, protecting registries, and rebuilding promptly when dependencies change.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:27.640
CI/CD permissions should not allow unreviewed workloads to bypass cluster policy.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:35.540
Network segmentation, node hardening, workload separation, runtime monitoring, and tested response complete the layered design.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.000
No individual control guarantees containment.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:45.340
The system is strongest when preventive controls reduce opportunity, detective controls reveal deviation, and architecture limits impact.
